findings.body:
`SettingsTextFormatter.formatStudiesText` calls `String(format: strings.detailTextStudies, appName)`, which is the old v1 copy. The PR adds `detailTextStudiesV2` a few lines above with the new "randomly selects users" text, but the helper never uses it. Anyone who adopts this helper for the new toggle would silently ship the old description.

::diff{file="focus-ios/Blockzilla/UIComponents/UIConstants.swift" lines="417-431"}

::callout{type="warning"}
No caller exists yet, so this is latent. It should be fixed in this PR, or the helper removed, so it can't be adopted with the wrong key.

::suggestion{file="focus-ios/Blockzilla/UIComponents/UIConstants.swift" lines="423-424"}
    func formatStudiesText(appName: String) -> String {
        return String(format: strings.detailTextStudiesV2, appName)

The `SettingsTextFormatter` singleton has no callers. Its `private init()` and `static let shared` add ceremony for two stateless functions that duplicate `strings.detailTextStudies` lookups. `detailTextSendUsageDataV2`, `labelStudiesV2`, `labelRollouts` and `detailTextRollouts` are also unused. Keeping dead constants in `UIConstants` makes it hard to tell which keys are live when the toggle split lands.

::diff{file="focus-ios/Blockzilla/UIComponents/UIConstants.swift" lines="417-431"}

If the follow-up PR is what consumes these, consider adding them there. Otherwise, a plain `String(format:)` call at the call site is simpler.
